WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Dr. Khalifa: Now this is, I mean, Satan cannot say that these people are, are mine.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.000
He cannot say that.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
When they say,

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:21.000
[60:4] ... "We disown you and the idols you worship beside GOD. We denounce you, and you will see nothing from us except animosity and hatred until you believe in GOD ALONE."* ...

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000
And then, we're given the example of Abraham and his father.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:43.000
[60:4] ... However, a mistake was committed by Abraham when he said to his father, "I will pray for your forgiveness,** but I possess no power to protect you from GOD." "Our Lord, we trust in You; we submit to You; to You is the final destiny.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:53.000
[60:5] "Our Lord, let us not be oppressed by those who disbelieved, and forgive us. You are the Almighty, Most Wise."

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:12.000
So, I think we learn from this page that we just, our stand must be firm, and it reminds us that we are here.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:23.000
All this trouble is because we rebelled, we did not make a firm stand on the side of God when the Great Feud happened.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:32.000
The jinns, for example, made a firm stand with Satan, and we, we didn't.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:38.000
We said "maybe, maybe, Satan can make it and be a god."

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.000
We did not make a firm stand with God.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:49.000
So, this is our time to make up for it, and to denounce that wishy-washy stand that we had in the past.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Ok, verse 6.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:10.000
[60:6] A good example has been set by them for those who seek GOD and the Last Day. As for those who turn away, GOD is in no need (of them), Most Praiseworthy.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.000
[60:7] GOD may change the animosity between you and them into love. ...

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:23.000
You see, what I mean when I said make your firm, your stand known orally, publicly, and tell them

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:30.000
"it's ok, you can study and examine the evidence until God guides you.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.000
But make it known.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:40.000
[60:7] ... GOD is Omnipotent. GOD is Forgiver, Most Merciful.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.000
And these relationships are regulated by the next two verses.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.000
It tells you exactly how to behave towards whom.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.000
Number 8 says,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:03:08.000
[60:8] GOD does not enjoin you from befriending those who do not fight you because of religion, and do not evict you from your homes. You may befriend them and be equitable towards them. GOD loves the equitable.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.000
So, these are not considered the enemies of God if they are not actively opposing you.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:18.000
They may be curious. They may be still looking. They may be still examining the evidence.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.000
You'll be able to tell if they are hostile or not.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.000
Number 9 tells you that

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:39.000
[60:9] GOD enjoins you only from befriending those who fight you because of religion, evict you from your homes, and band together with others to banish you. You shall not befriend them. Those who befriend them are the transgressors.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:47.000
Dr. Khalifa: If you are friends of somebody who's opposing God and His Messenger, what does this tell about you?

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.000
A woman: (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: Yeah.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.000
A man: Wishy-washy.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:54.000
Dr. Khalifa: Hmm?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.000
A man: Wishy-washy. Dr. Khalifa: Yes. Or worse.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.000
A man: (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.000
Dr. Khalifa: You have to make your stand very firm on the side of God alone.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:16.000
If somebody is idolizing Muhammad or Jesus or Mary or some saint with God, you have to

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.000
make your stand known that you don't like that, that you are not their friends until

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.000
they abandon their idolatry and dedicate themselves to God alone.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.000
Otherwise, we will be like them.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.000
This is... throughout the Quran, we see this.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:37.000
If you don't, if you don't do that, you are like them, as guilty as they are.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.000
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible)

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:46.000
A man: Yeah. For example, you work in the same office for them and provided they don't follow you. You Pray own way.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.000
A man: they pray their own way and they don't follow you.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: Right. A man: They meet you in the same restaurant.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.000
Dr. Khalifa: Right.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:59.000
A man: You, you meet in the same clubs and all places, play the same game in a place in the evening. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.000
A man: Provided they follow you...

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: They don't bother you, they're not fighting you. Then,...

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.000
A man: Yeah, you can talk to them. A man: They're neutral.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes. A man: Neutral. Yes.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: They're neutral. There's still, there's still hope for them.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, there's no problem you talk to them, you play around, joke with them, (unintelligible) aside? Dr. Khalifa: Exactly.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.000
Dr. Khalifa: Exactly.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:22.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yeah, verses 8 and 9 are really, are the rule that covers, the umbrella rule.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:27.000
A man: Can we do (unintelligible)?

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.000
Dr. Khalifa: If they're still, if they're still neutral, yes.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: Especially, if it's going to help them.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:42.000
A man: Surely, if they declare themselves, declare themselves that they are non-believers, can we do good to them?

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, you better run away from them.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.000
Dr. Khalifa: If they declare themselves as non-believers, you better...

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.000
A man: If they need help, one kind or the other...

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:00.000
A man: Help, some kind of, shall we help them?

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.000
Dr. Khalifa: Not if they declare themselves as unbelievers. They're enemies of God. Yes. A man: They have. They have.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, you have to run, run away from them.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.000
Dr. Khalifa: You don't help them. A man: Don't help them? Dr. Khalifa: No.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is what, let's read it again.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.000
Number 9,

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:24.000
[60:9] GOD enjoins you from befriending those who fight you because of religion, evict you from your homes, and band together with others to banish you. ...

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:28.000
Better yet, if you look at verse number 1, it says,

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:31.000
[60:1] O you who believe, you shall not befriend My enemies and your enemies, ...

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:36.000
So, a person who declared himself as an unbeliever is an enemy of God.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.000
It shows the opposite side.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:47.000
Unless you have something else in mind as far as declare themselves unbelievers.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.000
Dr. Khalifa: Can you be more specific?

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.000
Edip: For sure. I mean, excuse me.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:58.000
Edip: How a person can be, can be included in number verse 8?

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.000
Edip: These are not believers, in fact.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: But they're neutral. Edip: They are disbelievers.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:08.000
Edip: And they are not actively fighting against believers. In the...

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:16.000
Edip: Because in number 8, there are some people that they are not believers, but they do not believe

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:25.000
or maybe they are agnostic, maybe they are Christian or Jews, they worship, but they have not animosity, how do you say, enmity.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.000
Edip: They're (unintelligible). Dr. Khalifa: There's no fighting, in other words.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.000
Edip: They don't fight.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.000
Dr. Khalifa: Will this define what you mean?

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.000
A man: Exactly.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:47.000
A man: Here, "extending love and friendship to them", but there is a, there is a wide margin between love and friendship.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:55.000
A man: I personally as a good Muslim would like to love my enemy.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:05.000
A man: I do not know whether that enemy is the enemy of God, but it says both, "your enemies and My enemies."

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:13.000
A man: But I am specifying that there is a person, I know that he's my enemy.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:19.000
I wouldn't call anyone my enemy, but I would say that this man has done bad to me.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.000
I would like to love him.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.000
A man: I would respond by loving him.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:29.000
Dr. Khalifa: Cause you're enemy like in work, there are circumstances. So,...

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:39.000
Dr. Khalifa: Unless he goes a little too far by, as it says that, take my house, take my home away,

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:44.000
A man: then of course, I would retaliate differently.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:50.000
Dr. Khalifa: Ok, if it is, if it is personal friction, the Quran actually tells you to love your enemy. A man: Yeah.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:56.000
Dr. Khalifa: I mean, if it's a personal matter, like, for example, he built his fence A man: Yes.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:02.000
Dr. Khalifa: inside your territory instead of, you know, half yard inside your territory or something, this has nothing to do with God.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:07.000
And in fact, I don't know if the Arabic will mean anything to you,

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.000
(28:54) يَدْرَءُونَ بِٱلْحَسَنَةِ ٱلسَّيِّئَةَ

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:12.000
In other words, if something does bad to you, you do good to them.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.000
Perhaps he will become your friend in the future.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:20.000
Dr. Khalifa: But here, we're talking strictly religion, as far as worshipping God alone is concerned.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.000
A man: Yes.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, when you say "my enemy..."

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:29.000
A man: The ultimate would be that he may turn to be a believer, because I am a believer. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:36.000
Dr. Khalifa: Right, if you mean by "my enemy", personal animosity, that is, the Quran tells you to do good to them, to love your enemy.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:43.000
But, because you'll be fighting for your sake, not for God's sake.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:48.000
This is why the verse starts with "My enemies." God is saying "My enemies" first.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: [60:1] ... you shall not befriend My enemies and your enemies, ...

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.000
Edip: The God's enemies also show our enemies.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.000
Dr. Khalifa: That's right.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:56.000
A woman: Because (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: So,

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: the love and hate should be for the sake of God, not for our personal sake.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:04.000
Feroz: And these are not all idol worshippers, it's only the ones that are actively fighting.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:05.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:11.000
Dr. Khalifa: You know, let us face it, when we grew up, they taught us idolatry, idol worship.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:16.000
We grew up as idol worshippers, all of us, this generation anyway.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:19.000
The new generation is cleaner than we are.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:23.000
But, you give them a chance to see the truth.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:29.000
So, if they're not fighting you, there is hope that someday they may be better than you and me.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.000
A man: But... Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:36.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:43.000
A man: Yes, I was telling you, stay in the same office, you share the same restaurant and all these things,

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:50.000
and they are neutral, and they happen to be in need of some help.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:52.000
A man: Now, won't you help them in such a situation?

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.000
Dr. Khalifa: You help them if they're not fighting you.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: If they're not actively fighting you, you help them, yes.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:01.000
A man: And in case, I mean, they need your help.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:06.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, look on them as potential believers. You're trying to woo them, actually. A man: Ok. Yeah.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.000
A man: Ok. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:09.000
A man: You can help them in such a situation. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.000
A man: You can befriend them, help them.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:14.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is what verse 8 is saying. It says,

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:20.000
[60:8] GOD does not prohibit you from befriending those who are not fighting you..., and not evicting you from your homes. ...

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.000
[60:8] ... fighting you because of religion, ...

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.000
Dr. Khalifa: Excuse me, I have to add those three words.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:25.000
A man: Yeah.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because of religion, not because of personal matters.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:35.000
A woman: Rashad, throughout the Quran, we see that we need that we should respect the relatives.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:39.000
Dr. Khalifa: Regard, regard the relatives. A woman: Regard, regard the relatives.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:43.000
A woman: And if one of our relatives is idol worshipper.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:48.000
Dr. Khalifa: You disown them. No, no, excuse me, go on, "I'm fighting you." I'm sorry. Yes.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:55.000
A woman: If they, if they declare that they believe in, they put Muhammad beside God. They declare... Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: But they are not fighting you.

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:59.000
A woman: But they are not fighting you. Dr. Khalifa: Fine, it's ok.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:05.000
A woman: It's fine? Dr. Khalifa: You can be their friends and love them and everything and try, try to woo them to worshiping God alone.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.000
A man: (31:15) وَإِن جَـٰهَدَاكَ Because

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:09.000
A man: (31:15) وَإِن جَـٰهَدَاكَ

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.000
A man: That time, there'll be problem.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.000
Dr. Khalifa: (31:15) لَا تُطِعْهُمَا

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.000
Dr. Khalifa: They don't even fight you. A man: Yes.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is about the parents.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:18.000
A man: Only if they struggle against you.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yeah. No, she's talking about relatives, like cousins, cousins, aunts, nephews, nieces. A woman: Yeah.

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: Right?

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:27.000
A man: Even if your parents, if they fight you, you still have to respect them.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:28.000
Dr. Khalifa: That's right.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:35.000
Dr. Khalifa: But you don't, you don't obey them in that particular idol worshipping situation. A man: in that particular.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.000
A woman: Is there any difference between which relatives that you're asking?

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:42.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yeah, the parents have a special position.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.000
Dr. Khalifa: The parents, God says "don't say 'Uff' to them."

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.000
A woman: Alright. But you say if they're idol worshipping, we should...

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:55.000
Dr. Khalifa: But, but God gives you permission to disobey them if they are forcing you to commit idolatry.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:58.000
They say "you must mention Muhammad and Ibrahim in your Prayer", for example.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:00.000
You don't obey them.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:09.000
You say "ok, mom or dad, I just keep, I understand your opinion and I appreciate your situation, but I'll do it my way. It's my neck."

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:19.000
A woman: Yes, it's like mine is saying... They disagree with my being here, but they're not being (unintelligible).

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:25.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because they don't know anything about us anyway. A woman: No. They just, they just kind of

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:31.000
A woman: accept them some information, but they don't, they don't wanna look at it. They just (unintelligible).

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:40.000
Dr. Khalifa: Ok, let's see what the rest of the Sura says, verse 10. In Case of War

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:53.000
[60:10] O you who believe, when believing women (abandon the enemy and) ask for asylum with you, you shall test them. GOD is fully aware of their belief. Once you establish that they are believers, you shall not return them to the disbelievers.

00:13:53.000 --> 00:14:08.000
[60:10] ...They are not lawful to remain married to them, nor shall the disbelievers be allowed to marry them. Give back the dowries that the disbelievers have paid. You commit no error by marrying them, so long as you pay them their due dowries.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:22.000
[60:10] ...Do not keep disbelieving wives (if they wish to join the enemy). You may ask them for the dowry you had paid, and they may ask for what they paid. This is GOD's rule; He rules among you. GOD is Omniscient, Most Wise.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:30.000
This probably will not, will never apply to us, but what this is saying is when two camps are fighting,

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:38.000
one camp are disbelievers, another camp is believers, and some, some women on the disbelievers' side join the believers,

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:42.000
you do not have to obtain an, an official divorce for the women.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:48.000
You can consider them divorced without, without any official action.

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:55.000
And the same if women from the believers' side decide to disbelieve and join the disbelievers' camp,

00:14:55.000 --> 00:15:00.000
God is actually telling the believers to give them back their dowries and divorce them.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.000
If this is what they want.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.000
Number 11,

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.000
[60:11] If any of your wives join the enemies' ...

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.000
Oh, I was a little ahead of myself.

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:25.000
[60:11] If any of your wives join the enemies' camp, and you are forced to fight, you shall force the enemy to compensate the men who lost their wives, by giving them what they spent on their wives. You shall reverence GOD, in whom you believe.

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:26.000
Number 12,

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:52.000
[60:12] O you prophet, when the believing women (who abandoned the disbelievers) to seek asylum with you pledge to you that they will not set up any idols besides GOD, nor steal, nor commit adultery, nor kill their children, nor fabricate any falsehood, nor disobey your righteous orders, you shall accept their pledge, and pray to GOD to forgive them. GOD is Forgiver, Most Merciful.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:58.000
Now, when number 12 says "O you prophet", what does this tell us?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because this is at the time of the prophet Muhammad. It is not applicable to us. A man: (unintelligible). Yes.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:09.000
Starting at verse 10.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:10.000
Number 13,

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:14.000
[60:13] O you who believe, do not befriend people with whom GOD is angry, ...

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:17.000
This repeats verse 1 and verse 9.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:25.000
[60:13] O you who believe, do not befriend people with whom GOD is angry, and who are hopelessly stuck in disbelief; ...

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:29.000
It's very important, "hopelessly stuck in disbelief."

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:34.000
You have to use your own judgement if the person, if there is hope that the person may become a believer or not.

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:43.000
And if there is hope that the person may become a believer, you better be as diplomatic as you can to help them.

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:48.000
You have, you have a lot at stake, by the way, when you do that.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:53.000
Because when you help somebody come to the truth, you get a lot of credit.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:17:02.000
So, God gives us incentives, lots of positive incentives to do that.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:07.000
So, if you sense that the person is, there is hope that the person may become a believer,

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:11.000
Dr. Khalifa: you should be as diplomatic as can be, and you use your own judgement in that.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:20.000
A woman: This, so, (unintelligible)

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: But there is no war. Yeah. This is in case of war.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.000
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:28.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, yes I know.

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:31.000
Dr. Khalifa: They do all kinds of strange things.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:32.000
A man: Al-Salaamu ‘Alaykum

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: Hey!

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:35.000
Parivash: Wow! Mã Shã Allãh.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:39.000
Dr. Khalifa: You made it!

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.000
A woman: Wow.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.000
A woman: Wow.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.000
Dr. Khalifa: Come on in, come on in.

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:47.000
A woman: Alhamdu Lillah

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:54.000
A woman: Salam.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:56.000
Parivash: Salam Dr. Khalifa: Salam. Come on, here, here, come here.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:10.000
A man: Oh, excellent!

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:12.000
A man: Hi!

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:15.000
People: Salam.

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:16.000
A woman: Alhamdu Lillah

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:18.000
A man: Sorry, (unintelligible)

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, no, it's fine.

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:22.000
A man: The door was locked but (unintelligible).

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:25.000
Dr. Khalifa: "With whom God is angry", these are your criteria.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:29.000
[60:13] ... and who are hopelessly stuck in disbelief; ...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:36.000
[60:13] ... hopelessly stuck in disbelief; they are just as hopeless as the disbelievers who are already in the graves.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:41.000
In other words, there's absolutely no hope for them, therefore you cannot, you cannot defend them.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:44.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is why you have to use your own judgement.

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:46.000
A man: Patience.

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:47.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:49.000
A man: (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:50.000
A man: So, give up.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.000
Dr. Khalifa: There he is, he's here.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:56.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is Mardana. Mardana: Very glad to be here.

00:18:56.000 --> 00:19:00.000
Dr. Khalifa: The Canadian group were asking about you.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.000
Behrouz: Yes. I hug everybody later.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:05.000
Behrouz: Hi, how are you?

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:07.000
A woman: You promise?

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:11.000
Behrouz: Yes, yes. If you accept our dirty clothes and...

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.000
A woman: Yes.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:15.000
Behrouz: Ok.

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:20.000
Dr. Khalifa: Let us finish the page, page 551.

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:24.000
The Sura 61, "The Column (Al-Suff)"

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:27.000
In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:32.000
[61:1] Glorifying GOD is everything in the heavens and everything on earth. ...

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.000
Think about that.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:37.000
Can we, can we keep the kids quiet somehow?

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:42.000
Tell them to lower their voices.

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:48.000
[61:1] Glorifying GOD is everything in the heavens and everything on earth. ...

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:54.000
The carpet, walls, glorifying God.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.000
I think we went into details of this before.

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:06.000
It was a kind of surprise.

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:08.000
This carpet is made of certain atoms.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:11.000
And every atom has certain number of electrons.

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:15.000
And electrons are rotating in specific orbits.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:19.000
And this is God's law. So, they are glorifying God.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:21.000
In Sura 17, God says,

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.000
(17:44) وَإِن مِّن شَىْءٍ إِلَّا يُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِهِۦ

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:25.000
There is nothing that does not glorify God.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:27.000
Even the disbelievers.

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: And the rest of the verse here says "we do not understand their glorification."

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.000
A man: Right.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:42.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, the disbelievers' bodies, disbelievers cannot control the heartbeats, or the lungs breathing.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.000
Feroz: Only difference is they're doing it unwillingly.

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:45.000
Dr. Khalifa: Right.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:49.000
Edip: Rashad, God gives an interesting example of shadow. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:51.000
Edip: God says, (unintelligible)

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:59.000
Edip: They think that disobey God, but their shadow obeys God's rule and so (unintelligible)

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:02.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes. I was just writing a footnote about this yesterday.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:06.000
And I said that the solar clocks bear witness to that.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:12.000
There's, there is a solar clock here in the university in front of the observatory.

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:17.000
And it's very accurate because it's based on the shadow.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:20.000
It tells you exactly what time it is.

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:23.000
It's an eternal clock.

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:25.000
So,

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:32.000
[61:1] Glorifying GOD is everything in the heavens and everything on earth. He is the Almighty, Most Wise.

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:36.000
[61:2] O you who believe, why do you say what you do not do?

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:42.000
[61:3] Most abominable in the sight of GOD is that you say what you do not do.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:47.000
So, if you're asking somebody to do the five Prayers, you better be doing them yourself.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:52.000
Number four,

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:59.000
[61:4] GOD loves those who fight in His cause to be united in one column, like the bricks in one wall.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:06.000
There is no, there shouldn't be any, any differences.

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:09.000
We have to be one.

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:14.000
This is why we see in Sura 6 that God condemns sectarianism.

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:21.000
God says, says "those who divide the religion into sects do not belong to God or the prophet."

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:32.000
And they, they hear this practically every day. But they still say "I'm a Shafe'i, I'm a Malki, I'm a Hanbali, I'm a Sunni, I'm a Shia, Ahmadi."

00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:34.000
A man: (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:41.000
Dr. Khalifa: Barbara, what are you?

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:45.000
Barbara: A submitter, Rashad. Dr. Khalifa: Mã Shã Allãh, yes.

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:50.000
Dr. Khalifa: I don't think we have any trouble under this roof saying who we are.

00:22:50.000 --> 00:23:00.000
A woman: A lot of people (unintelligible). A lot of them, they just say "Well, this is not (unintelligible)"

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's the only thing they know.

00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:11.000
Dr. Khalifa: But you go to any typical masjid in any Muslim country, and under the same roof you're gonna find different sects.

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:14.000
Edip: Oh, today, Rashad, that Arab came.

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:15.000
Dr. Khalifa: Is he an Arab?

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:16.000
Edip: Yes, he was Yemeni.

00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:17.000
Dr. Khalifa: Uh-uh.

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:28.000
Edip: And he came before, he said, he came, he said, "now this masjid, that masjid, there are a lot of hatred and bad things."

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:31.000
"I hate that, I don't like, I want to make search, research."

00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:35.000
Edip: And he came here, only for this reason, they have trouble there.

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:38.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, they always do. They have fistfights.

00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:40.000
This is in every masjid.

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:41.000
I know.

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:48.000
So, this Sura is entitled "Al-Suff (The Column)."

00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:51.000
Like the bricks in one wall.

00:23:51.000 --> 00:24:03.000
[61:5] Recall that Moses said to his people, "O my people, why do you hurt me, even though you know that I am GOD's messenger to you?" When they deviated, GOD diverted their hearts. For GOD does not guide the wicked people.

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:08.000
So, that's it.

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:11.000
And then, we open to general discussions.

00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:15.000
Dr. Khalifa: Any questions, Azar?

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:16.000
Azar: No.

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:18.000
Dr. Khalifa: I don't believe it.

00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:25.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yesterday, I asked "do you have any questions?" She said "how are you?"

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:36.000
Parivash: (6:159) إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ فَرَّقُوا۟ دِينَهُمْ وَكَانُوا۟ شِيَعًۭا

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:39.000
Parivash: 6:1.. Dr. Khalifa: 6:159

00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:40.000
Parivash: 159

00:24:42.000 --> 00:24:44.000
A woman: Dr. Khalifa, I have a question.

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:51.000
A woman: Is there any specific rule that men always have to prepare for the (unintelligible)? Just the (unintelligible)

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:55.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is the way that came to us all the way from Abraham.

00:24:55.000 --> 00:25:01.000
And usually, if God wants to set a precedent for the subsequent generations,

00:25:01.000 --> 00:25:10.000
God would create a situation or circumstances that will force this issue and then we'll have a precedent that a woman is leading the Prayer.

00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:15.000
But that never happened, and the innovations are a very serious matter.

00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:21.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, just so, not start any innovation, we're keeping this, this rule.

00:25:22.000 --> 00:25:28.000
A woman: But I think in my own house, does my father always have to prepare (unintelligible)?

00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: I would say "yes", because of this same reason.

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:39.000
This has been always the rule, and any change in it would be an innovation.

00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:43.000
So, it's not worth it. It's not worth it.

00:25:43.000 --> 00:25:55.000
But from the logical point of view, a woman leading the Prayer is not, is not... the woman is dignified, and it'll be more distracting for the men.

00:26:03.000 --> 00:26:05.000
It's very dangerous to start a new innovation, something new.

00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:08.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:13.000
A man: There's, there are 2 places that...

00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: That's a bad question.

00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:19.000
A man: We're talking about... Dr. Khalifa: No, no, go ahead.

00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:21.000
A man: We're talking about cuts in Quran.

00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:26.000
A man: One is when they're cutting the thief's hand. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:30.000
A man: The other one when Joseph, those ladies cut their hands because of...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:40.000
A man: And there's a third one that Pharaoh tells those people who follow Moses, says "I will cut your hands and feet on alternate sides."

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:41.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:46.000
A man: Oh, I don't know, but I mean, my question is, is the third one similar to the first or the second? Dr. Khalifa: No.

00:26:47.000 --> 00:26:49.000
A man: So I... Dr. Khalifa: It's neither.

00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:49.000
A man: Pardon?

00:26:49.000 --> 00:27:00.000
Dr. Khalifa: The word used for Joseph and the women, and 19 verses later in Sura Joseph, and also cutting the hand of the thief, that's the same word.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:01.000
A man: The same word.

00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: But the word used for the people who commit gross crimes and fight God, and the word that Pharaoh is using is different.

00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:14.000
It's Qatte'a (قَطِّعَ) and Qatta'a (قَطَّعَ)

00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:15.000
Dr. Khalifa: You see the difference?

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:17.000
A man: Well, I don't know. I don't understand.

00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:22.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, no, listen, listen, just listen to the word. Qatta'a (قَطَّعَ), this is the root for the hand of the thief.

00:27:23.000 --> 00:27:26.000
Dr. Khalifa: But for the people who commit gross crimes, it's Qatte'a (قَطِّعَ).

00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:30.000
A man: So, the thief and Joseph, basically exactly the same. Dr. Khalifa: Right.

00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: Same word, exactly.

00:27:32.000 --> 00:27:33.000
A man: What's the fourth one?

00:27:34.000 --> 00:27:36.000
Edip: It is, Rashad said. Dr. Khalifa: Qatte'a (قَطِّعَ).

00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:41.000
Edip: The people that fight against believers, they could be killed and also...

00:27:41.000 --> 00:27:43.000
A man: No, that's the same one that Pharaoh used. Edip: Yes, that is...

00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:45.000
Dr. Khalifa: They commit heinous crimes.

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: Stealing is a very specific crime.

00:27:51.000 --> 00:27:59.000
Edip: Yes, the difference is very important because this root, Qatte'a (قَطِّعَ), is strongly punishment. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:27:59.000 --> 00:28:04.000
Edip: (unintelligible), It is to make it stronger. Dr. Khalifa: That's right.

00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:07.000
Edip: The other is Qatta'a (قَطَّعَ).

00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: God gave us mathematical evidence, so...

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.000
A woman: Rashad. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:21.000
A woman: Earlier this afternoon when we were studying, a question came up about Jumu‘ah, Jumu'ah Prayer.

00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:32.000
A woman: If you came in and the first, part of the first Khutba was given already, how many Rak'ats do you have to make?

00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: Two.

00:28:33.000 --> 00:28:34.000
A woman: Ok.

00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:41.000
Edip: You missed... A woman: Could you talk about, elaborate a little bit because it wasn't a very forward answer?

00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:44.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is a straightforward answer.

00:28:44.000 --> 00:28:50.000
Dr. Khalifa:If you miss the whole Khutba and come, the people haven't done the two Rak'ats, you do only two Rak'ats. Edip: Yes.

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because you went to the place and chances are you're gonna ask the people what was the subject, what did they talk about.

00:28:58.000 --> 00:28:59.000
It will, it will be discussed.

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:07.000
Dr. Khalifa: Also, you're Praying in a congregation. So, the credit carries over, in other words.

00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:09.000
A woman: Ok. Thank you.

00:29:10.000 --> 00:29:13.000
A woman: If you're alone on Friday... Dr. Khalifa: You cannot Pray. A woman: Then, you do 4?

00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:15.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:18.000
A man: So, even though you missed the whole thing...

00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:20.000
Dr. Khalifa: You give yourself a Khutba, you'll be accused of being schizo.

00:29:25.000 --> 00:29:28.000
So, the word Jumu'ah by definition is group.

00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:41.000
Yes, go ahead. You have a guest for one night, Azhar and Shahrukh.

00:29:41.000 --> 00:29:42.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because you came too early.

00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:43.000
A man: She's over there. A man: She just...

00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:46.000
A man: She's over there. Dr. Khalifa: Go ahead. A man: Yes.

00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:47.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, she... A man: She's...

00:29:47.000 --> 00:29:50.000
A man: (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: No, she wasn't.

00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: There she is.

00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:54.000
A man: (unintelligible) A man: Mã Shã Allãh.

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:56.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:59.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yeah, go ahead. Do you need people to help you move in?

00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:01.000
A man: No, no, tomorrow.

00:30:01.000 --> 00:30:05.000
Dr. Khalifa: We have great muscles, see? Sheikh Mahmoud's muscles, and (unintelligible) and Edip's.

00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:08.000
A man: In fact, tomorrow IN SHAA ALLAH, we have to (unintelligible).

00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:12.000
A man: Or you have a truck. Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible)

00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:14.000
A man: A truck.

00:30:14.000 --> 00:30:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: Just say when. Tomorrow morning?

00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:17.000
A man: Yes. We have to... Dr. Khalifa: Tonight?

00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:21.000
A man: No, not tonight because they're closed. We have to take (unintelligible).

00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:23.000
A man: I'm pulling my car with it.

00:30:23.000 --> 00:30:24.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:26.000
Dr. Khalifa: Ok. A man: And then bring his car back.

00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:28.000
Dr. Khalifa: Just say when and we'll be here, IN SHAA ALLAH.

00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:30.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:32.000
A man: He's gone. Dr. Khalifa: No, he's gone.

00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:34.000
A man: Thank you.

00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:39.000
A woman: .... this life because...

00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:41.000
A woman: (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: Exactly.

00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:43.000
Edip: May I say something?

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:44.000
Dr. Khalifa: Go ahead.

00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:54.000
Edip: This is a good point. But if you think further, God is capable to create a system that even if everybody live well

00:30:54.000 --> 00:31:05.000
Edip: and also can they survive. God is, it's God's system now we're talking about, but God can create another, create another system that even everybody could survive on the earth.

00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:07.000
Dr. Khalifa: But we're talking about the system we have now. Edip: Ok.

00:31:08.000 --> 00:31:10.000
Edip: But it is possible for God.

00:31:10.000 --> 00:31:14.000
But why God decided on the system.

00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:18.000
I have also additionally another answer.

00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:27.000
The final is the most, the important thing, the test, the (unintelligible) test, worship God alone.

00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:31.000
Everything, for example, to be poor or to be rich.

00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:40.000
You just see many rich people, they do not see the message because they are rich, they are proud, they don't involve, they don't take care.

00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:42.000
But many poor people, they accept.

00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:50.000
Sometimes differently in this test, all poor to be poor or to be rich has the same disadvantage and advantage.

00:31:51.000 --> 00:31:59.000
And if you look at the perspective of the test and the final result, they all have the same,

00:31:59.000 --> 00:32:04.000
Edip: I'd say different but equal problems and equal advantages.

00:32:04.000 --> 00:32:06.000
Dr. Khalifa: What is, what is happening to communism today?

00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:09.000
Communism failed.

00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:15.000
Where Karl Marx said "everybody has... all people have to be equal."

00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:16.000
It didn't work.

00:32:17.000 --> 00:32:19.000
Nasser destroyed Egypt using this principle.

00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:25.000
Because all of a sudden the boss will call somebody to do something.

00:32:25.000 --> 00:32:28.000
"No, I'm not gonna do it. I'm just as... I'm just like you."

00:32:29.000 --> 00:32:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: And the whole country stopped from that moment.

00:32:32.000 --> 00:32:40.000
A man: Rashad, I think if the system was like, like Edip said, everything was equal and so on and

00:32:40.000 --> 00:32:48.000
A man: God would make it work also the other way, then we would have some (unintelligible) not just this world. (unintelligible)

00:32:52.000 --> 00:32:53.000
A man: He's right. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:32:53.000 --> 00:33:00.000
